Position Summary

Centro Medico Community Clinic is seeking a hands-on, technology-oriented AI & Operations Systems Coordinator to take day-to-day ownership of the CMCC Portal, our developing internal operations and management platform.

CMCC leadership has already developed the foundation and workflows for the portal. We are looking for someone who can take that foundation, support our users, understand operational needs, continuously improve workflows, and help develop new functionality using modern AI-assisted development tools.

Experience working with Claude or similar AI coding/development tools is strongly preferred.

This is not a traditional IT help-desk position and does not require a senior software-engineering résumé. We are looking for someone who understands technology, learns quickly, enjoys building things, can troubleshoot problems, and can work directly with staff to turn operational needs into practical solutions.

Reports To: COO

Strategic Oversight: CEO

Works Closely With: Information/Technology, Operations, Leadership and outside IT resources

Key Responsibilities

· Serve as the day-to-day owner and administrator of the CMCC Portal.

· Provide ongoing portal support to employees and managers.

· Understand existing portal architecture, workflows and functionality.

· Use Claude and other AI-assisted development tools to help develop, modify and improve portal functionality.

· Translate operational requests into practical workflows and system improvements.

· Build and improve forms, dashboards, trackers, reporting tools and internal workflows.

· Troubleshoot portal issues and coordinate technical support when needed.

· Test new functionality before deployment.

· Maintain a prioritized list of portal improvements and development requests.

· Train employees and managers on portal functionality.

· Monitor portal adoption and identify departments that need additional support.

· Work directly with operational users to understand pain points and eliminate unnecessary manual processes.

· Document important workflows and system changes.

· Coordinate with CMCC IT and outside technical vendors when infrastructure or advanced technical support is required.

· Continually explore practical uses of AI and automation to improve CMCC operations.

Big-Picture KPIs

· Portal adoption and utilization

· User/support issues resolved

· Workflow completion

· Portal improvements successfully deployed

· Reduction of manual/repetitive processes

· User satisfaction and operational usefulness

Technical Skills We Value

· Practical experience using Claude for coding or application development

· Experience with AI-assisted coding tools or AI agents

· Ability to understand and modify existing code

· Basic understanding of web applications, databases, APIs and user permissions

· Ability to troubleshoot technical issues

· Understanding of workflow automation

· Ability to test and document system changes

· Comfortable learning unfamiliar technologies quickly

Knowledge of every programming language or technology is not required. The ability to understand an existing system, use AI effectively, troubleshoot, learn and safely make improvements is more important.

What We Are Looking For

· Curious and technically capable

· Strong problem-solving skills

· Highly organized

· Excellent follow-through

· Patient when supporting non-technical users

· Comfortable working directly with leadership and operations staff

· Team-oriented and collaborative

· Willing to learn instead of saying, “That’s not my area”

· Interested in AI, automation and improving how organizations work

· Healthcare experience is helpful but not required

Ideal Candidate

You are the person who enjoys figuring things out.

If someone says, “We do this manually every day—there has to be a better way,” your instinct is to understand the workflow, open Claude, explore a solution, test it, improve it and make it usable for the team.

We care more about your ability to learn, build, solve problems and work well with people than the size of your résumé.

